Z||000000||fierosound||01-13-2001||02:28 PM||||Those of you who've seen the TV series "Dark Skies" will be familair with Majestic 12.  Watchers of "X-Files" and "First Wave" will also find these documents extremely interesting.  Check them out...<BR> <A HREF="http://www.artbell.com/majestic.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.artbell.com/majestic.html</A> <p>[This message has been edited by fierosound (edited 01-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||01-13-2001||04:06 PM||||Im into UFO stuff a lot, Ive got almost every documentary ever made, most of the classic video sci fi too. I must have a hundred hours saved. I got to attend a Hogalin lecture, what he had to say about Mars and the Moon was very interesting. I had a first hand encounter in the mid 60's while I was in the AF-been a total believer ever since. Thanks for the link.||||reg||1
Z||000002||DaRkLoRD||01-13-2001||04:45 PM||||I've got a book by Stan Freidman (sp?) about the MJ-12 docs, as well as "the day after roswell" by Phillip Corso.. excellent books.<P>I'm not really into the whole UFO/Alien thing anymore, but I believe they exist, and have been visiting our planet for a long time.. possibly for tens of thousands of years.. (see Chariots of the Gods, by Erich von Daniken, Gods of the new Millennium by Allen Alford, anything by Zecharia Sitchin, etc..)<P>It might not be my primary interest right now, but I'm always up for a UFO discussion.. if anyone's interested, email me..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||14
Z||000003||Cliff Pennock||01-13-2001||05:48 PM||||I've always been interested in the UFO phenomena. Never had an encounter of any kind but the whole idea is pretty intriguing.<P>"Millions of people believe in God but nobody ever saw Him. Nobody believes in UFO's although millions see them each day"<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroJoe||01-13-2001||06:22 PM||||Given the size of the universe, and all its contents, and the theory that new parts of the universe are being added constantly (I'm more into the cosmos than UFO's), I think it would just be selfish to think that us Earth inhabitants are alone in this vast expanse.  So of course there is other intelligent life out there, if there wasnt, I'd say that that would be pretty queer.  And all the more better if they have been visiting us, hopefully they are peaceful and wish to share thier technology with us.||||reg||1
